import{_ as t,o as a,c as r,ag as o}from"./chunks/framework.KxDd3USm.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"11.8 精华题与补充题","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"11-专业英语/91-精华题与补充题.md","filePath":"11-专业英语/91-精华题与补充题.md"}'),s={name:"11-专业英语/91-精华题与补充题.md"};function n(i,e,c,l,d,p){return a(),r("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[o('<h1 id="_11-8-精华题与补充题" tabindex="-1">11.8 精华题与补充题 <a class="header-anchor" href="#_11-8-精华题与补充题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;11.8 精华题与补充题&quot;">​</a></h1><blockquote><p>限时 5 分钟完成。正式考试就是这种连续 5 空的形态。</p></blockquote><p>Continuous integration (CI) is a development practice in which programmers merge code changes into a shared repository <strong>(1)</strong>. Each change triggers an automated build and a set of tests. If a test fails, the team receives rapid <strong>(2)</strong> and can correct the problem while the change is still small. CI does not guarantee that software is defect-free; instead, it makes integration problems easier to <strong>(3)</strong> and locate. For CI to be effective, the build process should be repeatable and the test suite should run <strong>(4)</strong> without requiring manual steps. By finding defects early, a team reduces the risk that they will become more <strong>(5)</strong> to fix later.</p><p><strong>1.</strong> A. rarely　B. frequently　C. secretly　D. accidentally<br><strong>2.</strong> A. feedback　B. inheritance　C. encryption　D. storage<br><strong>3.</strong> A. detect　B. manufacture　C. postpone　D. authorize<br><strong>4.</strong> A. manually　B. automatically　C. visually　D. separately<br><strong>5.</strong> A. expensive　B. portable　C. atomic　D. available</p><h3 id="高频独立辨析题" tabindex="-1">高频独立辨析题 <a class="header-anchor" href="#高频独立辨析题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;高频独立辨析题&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>6.</strong> Authentication determines <strong>who a user is</strong>, while authorization determines（ ）。</p><p>A. how data is compressed<br> B. what the user is allowed to do<br> C. when a process is scheduled<br> D. where a packet is routed</p><p><strong>7.</strong> The phrase “high cohesion and low coupling” most directly describes（ ）。</p><p>A. desirable modular design<br> B. symmetric encryption<br> C. disk scheduling<br> D. database backup</p><hr><h2 id="补充题-真题标杆专项-不破坏原题编号" tabindex="-1">补充题（真题标杆专项，不破坏原题编号） <a class="header-anchor" href="#补充题-真题标杆专项-不破坏原题编号" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;补充题（真题标杆专项，不破坏原题编号）&quot;">​</a></h2><blockquote><p>先按正式考试方式限时 5 分钟做完，再看文末解析。</p></blockquote><h3 id="补充-passage-b-data-backup-and-recovery-第-b1–b5-题" tabindex="-1">补充 Passage B：Data Backup and Recovery（第 B1–B5 题） <a class="header-anchor" href="#补充-passage-b-data-backup-and-recovery-第-b1–b5-题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;补充 Passage B：Data Backup and Recovery（第 B1–B5 题）&quot;">​</a></h3><p>Backup is the process of copying data to a secondary location so that it can be restored after loss or damage. A common strategy keeps several copies, because a single copy provides little <strong>(B1)</strong> against media failure. Backups may be full, incremental, or differential; an incremental backup stores only the data that has changed <strong>(B2)</strong> the previous backup, saving time and space. Because restoring from incremental backups may require many tapes, organizations often combine them with periodic full backups. To be dependable, a backup plan must run <strong>(B3)</strong> on a schedule, and the restored data must be periodically <strong>(B4)</strong> to confirm it can actually be used. Finally, copies should be stored off site so that they survive a fire or other <strong>(B5)</strong>.</p><p><strong>B1.</strong> A. protection　B. machine　C. compiler　D. format<br><strong>B2.</strong> A. since　B. unless　C. before　D. into<br><strong>B3.</strong> A. manually　B. automatically　C. secretly　D. rarely<br><strong>B4.</strong> A. deleted　B. tested　C. encrypted　D. inherited<br><strong>B5.</strong> A. milestone　B. register　C. disaster　D. argument</p><h3 id="补充独立辨析题" tabindex="-1">补充独立辨析题 <a class="header-anchor" href="#补充独立辨析题" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;补充独立辨析题&quot;">​</a></h3><p><strong>C1.</strong> 下列句子中，<code>it</code> 指代的对象是（　）。</p><blockquote><p>The process sends the request to the server, and it responds with a cached copy.</p></blockquote><p>A. process　B. server　C. request　D. cached copy</p><p><strong>C2.</strong> 下列句子中，空格应填（　）。</p><blockquote><p>The data ___ from the file server, not the local disk.</p></blockquote><p>A. retrieved　B. retrieving　C. to retrieve　D. retrieves</p><hr>',23)])])}const g=t(s,[["render",n]]);export{u as __pageData,g as default};
